%% Slices decide implementation order and nothing else:
%%   s1 the bed map and the bed list   s2 adding rooms and beds   s3 blocking a bed
%% A flowchart rather than usecase-beta: see .claude/skills/feature-design/SKILL.md step b.
%% UML directions: include points base --> included. extend points extension --> base.
%% Refusals and contention are test cases, not use cases: they are rows in edge-cases.csv.
%% State transitions are in states.mmd and are deliberately not repeated here.
%%
%% Where it lives: under Front Office, gated by the front_desk capability. The daily
%% job here is a front-desk one — who is in each bed and which is free (blueprint 4.7,
%% front-desk mode) — and the map is what the booking form's Unit select is drawn from.
%% Blueprint 4.6 has no "Places" group and 5.2 is not Platform Core, so neither a new
%% top-level destination nor Configuration is the honest home. Writes are bounded by a
%% permission of their own (accommodation.configure), not by reaching the front desk.
flowchart TD

  DESK["Staff Member reaching the Property<br/>reads the map and the list"]
  CONFIG["Staff Member holding accommodation.configure<br/>adds rooms, blocks and unblocks"]
  RESIDENT["Resident<br/>reaches their own Unit through their Stay and no further (ADR 0009)"]

  subgraph S1["slice 1 &mdash; the bed map and the bed list"]
    MAP(["Read every Unit at a Property<br/>rooms with their beds, by building and floor"])
    OCC(["See who is in each Unit tonight<br/>in house, reserved, empty, blocked, out of service"])
    COUNT(["Read the counts<br/>rooms, sellable Units, in house, free, blocked"])
    LIST(["Read the same Units as a list<br/>searchable, one row per sellable Unit"])
  end

  subgraph S2["slice 2 &mdash; adding rooms and beds"]
    ADD(["Add rooms in one go<br/>building, floor, first number, how many, type, sleeps"])
    BEDS(["Let each new room by the bed<br/>one bed per sleeping place, named A, B, C&hellip;"])
  end

  subgraph S3["slice 3 &mdash; blocking a bed"]
    BLOCK(["Block a Unit with a reason<br/>it leaves the booking form and refuses check-in"])
    UNBLOCK(["Unblock it"])
  end

  subgraph OUT["Not this feature"]
    EDIT(["Rename a Unit, move it between floors, change its type or capacity"])
    REMOVE(["Remove a Unit that was never used"])
    HK(["Dirty, inspected, out of order &mdash; the housekeeping lifecycle (RANZ-28)"])
    MOVE(["Move a Stay to another Unit &mdash; transfers, refused by a column grant"])
    RACK(["Units against days &mdash; the room calendar (RANZ-25)"])
  end

  DESK --> MAP
  DESK --> LIST
  CONFIG --> ADD
  CONFIG --> BLOCK
  CONFIG --> UNBLOCK
  RESIDENT -.->|never| MAP

  MAP --> OCC
  MAP --> COUNT
  LIST --> OCC
  BEDS -->|extends| ADD
  BLOCK --> MAP
  UNBLOCK --> MAP
  ADD --> MAP

  %% OPEN: what a Staff Member does with a room added under the wrong number. This
  %% design blocks it with a reason and defers removal (RB-S3-12); a later slice may
  %% allow removing a Unit nothing has ever named.
